    content: "If you're a parent in Gurgaon Sector 78 looking at CBSE Tuition options, you've probably noticed the same thing: most centres claim they'll \"cover the syllabus\" and leave it at that. Good Marks Classes does cover the CBSE syllabus, but that's the baseline, not the point. The point is making sure your child actually understands it, gets tested on it regularly, and learns to write answers the way CBSE examiners award marks.\n\nWe're in Gurgaon Sector 78, which matters more than it sounds. A student who travels forty minutes to a class before sitting for a 7 PM session isn't fresh. Being close by is one of the reasons families around here choose us.\n\nThis is what our CBSE Tuition in Gurgaon Sector 78 actually looks like, day to day, class by class.\n\nWhat We Actually Teach, and How\n\nThe CBSE Tuition programme at Good Marks Classes is organised by class, because a Class 8 student and a Class 12 student have very different needs.\n\nClass 8 runs on a weekend-only timetable, deliberately. School and activities fill the week, so we don't add to it. Saturday holds 2 classes in the evening and Sunday holds 3 classes from morning to afternoon, 5 classes a week, covering Science, Mathematics, English and Social Studies along with olympiad and reasoning preparation. The idea is that a younger student builds strong fundamentals and writing habits without the week turning into a scramble.\n\nClasses 9 and 10 run on weekdays as well as weekends, because the board pressure is real and the syllabus is bigger. These batches focus on the CBSE syllabus itself, olympiad and NTSE preparation, weekly worksheet tests, and intensive subjective writing practice, which is the skill that quietly decides a huge share of board marks. Class 10 gets a board-first treatment with previous-year papers and mock board-style tests from early in the year.\n\nClasses 11 and 12 centre on Physics, Chemistry, Mathematics and Biology. Subject-specialist faculty teach each one, so a Physics doubt gets a Physics teacher's answer. Preparation is NCERT-first with board-pattern practice, and students are trained to frame answers the way examiners mark, show method steps, label diagrams, write to the word limit.\n\nWhy the Small-Batch Stuff Actually Matters\n\nA teacher with twenty students notices patterns, the same child mixing up the same formula three weeks running, or rushing through numericals without showing method. In a batch of sixty, that gets missed until a test score gives it away. Here it usually doesn't.\n\nWeekly worksheet tests keep progress honest, and they're scored and returned, not just assigned. Doubt sessions get actual time in the timetable. Parents get real updates on how their child is performing, not just a mark sheet every few months.\n\nThat's most of what CBSE Tuition in Gurgaon Sector 78 at Good Marks Classes is: consistent teaching, regular testing, honest feedback, and writing skills that students actually carry into the exam hall.\n\nCome See It Yourself\n\nA webpage only says so much. If this feels worth considering, sit in on an actual class. Talk to a teacher directly. Ask about the Class 8 weekend timetable or the Class 9 and 10 weekday-plus-weekend schedule, whichever fits. We'd rather earn that decision in person than through a page full of promises.\n\nCBSE Tuition in Gurgaon Sector 78: Good Marks Classes\n\nGood Marks Classes offers CBSE Tuition in Gurgaon Sector 78 for Classes 8 to 12, with small batches, subject-specialist faculty, weekly worksheet tests, olympiad and NTSE preparation, and focused subjective writing practice. Class 8 runs on a weekend-only schedule (Saturday evening and Sunday morning-to-afternoon), Classes 9 and 10 run on weekdays and weekends, and Classes 11 and 12 focus on Physics, Chemistry, Mathematics and Biology. Book a free demo class in Gurgaon Sector 78 and meet the teachers before you decide.",
